CORE
main.c
--all-properties
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .*assertion i==1: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .*assertion i==2: SUCCESS$
^\*\* 1 of 2 failed (2 iterations)$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The verdicts here have always been right: two threads each increment i inside
an atomic section and both are joined, so i==1 fails and i==2 holds.

What was stale is the expected output. --all-properties now exits 10 when any
property fails, not 0, and goto-checker/properties.cpp spells the per-property
results FAILURE and SUCCESS rather than FAILED and OK. The line number is
matched loosely so that editing main.c does not break this again.
